{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659798",
      "title": "Best Practice: Updating Object State Immutably",
      "sourceHash": "05d6cb283699bf235b064427ee4970becae75d5de168c80c4777dd897601e816",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.72,
          "en": "Now that we got the GameBoard component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.72,
          "end": 6.87,
          "en": "and we're dynamically rendering this grid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.87,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "it's time to make these buttons here work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.27,
          "en": "and to actually manage some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "for this gameboard so that it can change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 18.24,
          "en": "And so that we update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.24,
          "end": 21.93,
          "en": "and we place the symbol of the player who clicked a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.93,
          "end": 23.94,
          "en": "on the button that was clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.94,
          "end": 26.7,
          "en": "And therefore, here in this Gameboard component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.7,
          "end": 29.46,
          "en": "we of course want to add some new state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.46,
          "end": 32.28,
          "en": "which we can do with the useState hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.28,
          "end": 36.093,
          "en": "which of course must be imported from React as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.97,
          "end": 42.21,
          "en": "And the goal with this state here is to manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "and update the gameboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.49,
          "end": 47.34,
          "en": "Therefore, we can use this initialGameBoard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.34,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "as an initial value so that our state is such an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.69,
          "end": 55.833,
          "en": "of nested arrays, such a multidimensional array therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.15,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "And all name my state constant here gameBoard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 64.657,
          "en": "and the updating function setGameBoard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.02,
          "end": 68.82,
          "en": "And then we, of course, need a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 71.85,
          "en": "that can be triggered when this button here is pressed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "where we will update the state with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 77.133,
          "en": "of the setGameBoard function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 81.453,
          "en": "So here the function could be named handleSelectSquare",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.97,
          "end": 85.413,
          "en": "or something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "And when this is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 93.2,
          "en": "I want to call setGameBoard and replace my gameboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.47999999999999,
          "end": 98.22,
          "en": "with the new gameboard where one field will change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "from null to either an X or an O",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 104.85300000000001,
          "en": "depending on which player clicked this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.69,
          "end": 107.64,
          "en": "So therefore here, the goal of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.64,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "is to update the gameboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 113.64,
          "en": "based on the previous state of that gameboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.64,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "because of course we don't want to lose that previous state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 119.91,
          "en": "We don't wanna lose the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.91,
          "end": 122.37,
          "en": "about previously selected fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.37,
          "end": 126.003,
          "en": "We just want to update one field of this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 130.8,
          "en": "Hence here we should use this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.8,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "of updating the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 135.78,
          "en": "by passing a function to the state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "And we get our prevGameBoard as an argument here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "passed in automatically by React as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "And we want to return the updated gameboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.94,
          "end": 149.07,
          "en": "And for this and this function body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.07,
          "end": 153.18,
          "en": "of this inner function here, we want to replace one field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.18,
          "end": 156.753,
          "en": "in one of these inner arrays with an X or an O.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.01,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "Therefore here, handleSelectSquare",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 163.44,
          "en": "needs a couple of pieces of information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 166.68,
          "en": "We need to know which row index we have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.68,
          "end": 169.44,
          "en": "so which inner array contains the field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.44,
          "end": 173.85,
          "en": "that should be updated, which inner array was responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.85,
          "end": 176.28,
          "en": "for rendering this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.28,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "and of course then we need to know which exact field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 182.64,
          "en": "was clicked, so which null should be replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.64,
          "end": 185.28,
          "en": "with an X or an O.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.28,
          "end": 188.13,
          "en": "And for that here we can get the callIndex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.13,
          "end": 190.62,
          "en": "So that we got row and column.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.62,
          "end": 193.14,
          "en": "And then of course we also need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.14,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "which symbol should be placed there, an X or an O,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 200.52,
          "en": "though that, of course, will simply depend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.52,
          "end": 203.79,
          "en": "on whose player's turn it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.79,
          "end": 207.24,
          "en": "And we'll therefore take care about that a little bit later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.24,
          "end": 210.36,
          "en": "since we'll need to add some extra logic for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.36,
          "end": 212.4,
          "en": "So for the moment we'll simply use an X",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.4,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "for the field identified by these two indexes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 220.47,
          "en": "And therefore now we could take this prevGameBoard array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.47,
          "end": 223.14,
          "en": "and select one of these inner arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.14,
          "end": 225.48,
          "en": "with help of the rowIndex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.48,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "And then one of the elements inside of that inner array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 231.933,
          "en": "so one of these nulls here with help of the callIndex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 233.01,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "That's how we can get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 238.29,
          "en": "of one of these elements in our nested array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.29,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "And then we might want to overwrite this with an X",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 245.193,
          "en": "and then return this updated state here as our new state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 250.08,
          "en": "Now we could do this, but I'm saying could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.08,
          "end": 253.77,
          "en": "because this approach is not recommended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.77,
          "end": 255.9,
          "en": "Instead, just as you should use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.9,
          "end": 259.83,
          "en": "this state updating function when updating your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.83,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "based on some previous state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 266.31,
          "en": "it's also strongly recommended that if your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.31,
          "end": 270.42,
          "en": "is an object or array, you update that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.42,
          "end": 274.98,
          "en": "in an immutable way, which simply means you create a copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 274.98,
          "end": 279.98,
          "en": "of the old state, so a new object or a new array first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.35,
          "end": 282.96,
          "en": "and you then just change that copy instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 282.96,
          "end": 285.42,
          "en": "of that existing object or array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.42,
          "end": 287.76,
          "en": "And the reason for that recommendation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 287.76,
          "end": 291.15,
          "en": "is that if your state is an object or array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 291.15,
          "end": 294.96,
          "en": "you are dealing with a reference value in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.96,
          "end": 297.75,
          "en": "And therefore if you would be updating it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.75,
          "end": 302.13,
          "en": "you would be updating the old value in-memory immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 302.13,
          "end": 304.83,
          "en": "even before this scheduled state update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.83,
          "end": 307.32,
          "en": "was executed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 307.32,
          "end": 311.76,
          "en": "And this can again lead to strange bugs or side effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 311.76,
          "end": 315.27,
          "en": "if you have multiple places in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 315.27,
          "end": 319.41,
          "en": "that are scheduling state updates for the same state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 319.41,
          "end": 322.02,
          "en": "And in case this reference value thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 322.02,
          "end": 325.53,
          "en": "doesn't tell you anything, attached to this lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.53,
          "end": 327.72,
          "en": "you'll find a link to a resource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 327.72,
          "end": 329.37,
          "en": "that allows you to learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 329.37,
          "end": 332.25,
          "en": "about this crucial JavaScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 332.25,
          "end": 335.82,
          "en": "which you should know as a JavaScript developer in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 335.82,
          "end": 338.04,
          "en": "and which is especially important here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 341.433,
          "en": "when working with object or array state values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 342.69,
          "end": 344.76,
          "en": "So therefore here what we should do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.76,
          "end": 348.429,
          "en": "is create a new constant, or variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 348.429,
          "end": 350.73,
          "en": "updatedBoard could be the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 355.47,
          "en": "which is a new array where we can use the spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 355.47,
          "end": 360.47,
          "en": "to paste in all the existing elements of the old array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 362.52,
          "end": 366.24,
          "en": "So now this is technically a new array object in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366.24,
          "end": 370.443,
          "en": "that contains the old array elements as child elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 371.67,
          "end": 375.09,
          "en": "Now since here I'm dealing with some nest arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 375.09,
          "end": 379.74,
          "en": "those should be copied as well before we update anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 379.74,
          "end": 381.06,
          "en": "And we can achieve this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 381.06,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "by calling the map method on our old state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 387.6,
          "en": "so on our old array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 387.6,
          "end": 390.243,
          "en": "So that here we got our innerArrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 391.77,
          "end": 396.33,
          "en": "and for every innerArray we also return a new nested array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 396.33,
          "end": 400.413,
          "en": "which spreads the elements of that innerArray inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 401.90999999999997,
          "end": 405.27,
          "en": "So that technically here we got a brand new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 405.27,
          "end": 408.15,
          "en": "full of brand new nested arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 408.15,
          "end": 411.753,
          "en": "which still store the data they did store before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 412.92,
          "end": 417.06,
          "en": "but now it's this updated board that should be updated here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 417.06,
          "end": 418.563,
          "en": "and that should be returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 419.4,
          "end": 421.92,
          "en": "And by using this approach and pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 421.92,
          "end": 425.16,
          "en": "we are updating the state in an immutable way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 425.16,
          "end": 426.9,
          "en": "which is strongly recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 426.9,
          "end": 428.703,
          "en": "for the reasons mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 429.87,
          "end": 433.08,
          "en": "And with that, we can now use handleSelectSquare",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 433.08,
          "end": 436.683,
          "en": "and assign this to the onClick prop of this button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 438.6,
          "end": 443.43,
          "en": "Though, since we need row and callIndex as arguments here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 443.43,
          "end": 447.87,
          "en": "in handleSelectSquare, we want to use that trick, kind of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 447.87,
          "end": 450.45,
          "en": "I showed you earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 450.45,
          "end": 453.36,
          "en": "where we create a new anonymous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 453.36,
          "end": 456.96,
          "en": "which is then actually passed as a value to onClick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 456.96,
